Q. What is AWS?
A:	AWS (Amazon Web Services) is a cloud computing platform that provides on-demand services like computing, storage, databases, and networking.
It allows businesses to build, deploy, and scale applications without managing physical servers. 

Q. What are AWS Regions?
A:	An AWS Region is a geographical area that has multiple Availability Zones(AZs).
					OR
An AWS Region is a geographical area where AWS has data centers. Each region has multiple Availability Zones (AZs) to ensure reliability and low latency. 
Example: ap-south-1 (Mumbai) 2016 &  ap-south-2 (Hyderabad) 2022.


Q. What is the Availability Zone?
A:	An Availability Zone (AZ) is physically isolated and consists of one or more data centers, each data center containing multiple servers.
					OR
An Availability Zone (AZ) is a data center within an AWS Region. Each region has multiple AZs for high availability and fault tolerance.
Example: Mumbai Region (ap-south-1) has 3 Availability Zones (AZs): ap-south-1a , ap-south-1b , ap-south-1c.
Hyderabad Region (ap-south-2) has 3 Availability Zones (AZs): ap-south-2a , ap-south-2b , ap-south-2c.

Q. What is Edge Location?
A:	An Edge Location is a server near users that caches data for faster access. Used by CloudFront to speed up websites, videos, and APIs.
Example: If you watch a video, it loads from the nearest Edge Location instead of a far-away server.
