Q. What is Identity and Access Management (IAM)?
A:	AWS IAM (Identity and Access Management) lets you control who can access AWS resources and what actions they can perform.
IAM Components
Description
Example
Level / Usage
Users 👤
Individual accounts for people or services
A DevOps engineer accessing EC2
Identity-level (per user)
Groups 👥
A set of users with the same permissions
A "Developers" group with EC2 & S3 access
Identity-level (per group)


Roles 🎭 
Temporary permissions for AWS services or users
An EC2 instance using a role to access S3
Service/resource-level (temporary access)
Policies 📜
Rules that define what users, groups, and roles can do
A policy allowing "read-only" access to S3
Service/resource-level (defines allowed actions)

Q. AWS CLI and SDK Basics?
A:	AWS CLI (Command Line Interface) → A tool that lets you manage and automate AWS services using commands from the command-line.
AWS SDK (Software Development Kit) → A set of libraries that lets you Manage and Automate AWS Services using programming languages (Pythcon, Java, Node.js, etc.).
